# `plan` extracts the tree it gates here rather than into the session temp
# directory, because one of those gates measures where the tree is. Removed by
# promote.sh's own trap; ignored because a crash between the two leaves it.
.promote-plan.*

# Empty files named for a unix timestamp, which appeared in the root across four
# consecutive days and stopped. Nothing here creates them and nothing reads them.
#
# This line used to say "one per here-document, every session". That is wrong,
# and it is recorded rather than quietly replaced, because it is why nobody
# looked further for months: five here-document forms — redirected, captured,
# into a read loop, a herestring, into an interpreter — were each run sandboxed
# and unsandboxed and produced none.
#
# So the cause is unknown, and the pattern stays as a trap rather than an
# explanation. **If these reappear, write down when** — one span plus a confident
# wrong sentence identified nothing, and two spans would name what runs between
# them.
sh-thd-*

.DS_Store
*.local.json
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/orrery-calls.tsv
# The waiver log. Same reason as the line above, and it was learned the same
# way twice: a manual run of the guard wrote six rows into this file and
# `git add -A` committed them, so the first row of the record whose whole value
# is that its rows are true was a test artifact.
.claude/orrery-waivers.tsv
node_modules/

# Editor state — machine-specific, never shared
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/worktrees/
